    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d142-a2">

                <pb facs="0301" n="245" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg245"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 95.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hoffman to Lord Derby</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-05-20"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 20,
                        1876</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of yesterday in reference to the case of Winslow, and to
                    inform you that I have to-day telegraphed to Mr. Fish, in accordance with your
                    suggestion.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WICKHAM HOFFMAN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
